        "category": "api-contract",
        "title": "Unconditional bevy_camera dependency likely breaks no_std support",
        "explanation": "bevy_input_focus has std/critical-section/libm features, so it is meant to build on no_std targets. bevy_camera depends on rendering and asset crates (bevy_asset, bevy_image, bevy_mesh, etc.), which are probably not no_std-compatible. If so, adding it as a required dependency breaks the crate's no_std build and its CI check. It also pulls a heavy camera/asset dependency tree into a small input-focus crate. bevy_camera is also missing from the std, critical-section and bevy_reflect feature lists.",
        "suggestion": "Make bevy_camera optional behind a feature (e.g. `visibility = [\"dep:bevy_camera\"]`), use #[cfg] around the InheritedVisibility check, and forward the std/reflect features. Or move InheritedVisibility to a lighter crate.",
        "evidence": "bevy_camera = { path = \"../bevy_camera\", version = \"0.20.0-dev\", default-features = false }",
        "confidence": 0.55,
