        "start_line": 341,
        "end_line": 343,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Newly spawned entities skipped until visibility propagation runs",
        "explanation": "InheritedVisibility defaults to HIDDEN and is only computed by the visibility propagation system in PostUpdate. A focusable entity spawned with Visibility (e.g. a UI Node) in the current frame therefore reads as invisible. Tab navigation or `initialize` called before propagation (e.g. focusing the first element of a just-opened dialog) skips it, or returns NoFocusableEntities.",
        "suggestion": "Document this limitation, or treat entities whose InheritedVisibility was just added/changed this frame as visible. Alternatively check `Visibility` up the ancestor chain directly.",
        "evidence": "if inherited_visibility.is_none_or(|v| v.get())",
